From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] pathres: give an interposed package the my-unit of the device
 it sits on

handle-interposers links the interposed instance with an empty unit
address, so link-one falls back to the interposer's own "reg", which the
disk-label package doesn't have: my-unit of the instance that open-dev
returns for "cdrom" was 0 0. NetBSD's ofwboot reads the boot device's
target and lun with "my-unit" on that instance; with the IDE drives
addressed target,lun under the controller (cdrom@2,0, next patch) it got
target 0 and the kernel took wd0 instead of cd0 as its root device.

Copy the parent instance's my-unit into the interposed instance. With
this "cdrom" open-dev ... my-unit gives 0 2 and NetBSD 11.1 roots on cd0.
---
 forth/device/pathres.fs | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/forth/device/pathres.fs b/forth/device/pathres.fs
index a185b95..a2bf61c 100644
--- a/forth/device/pathres.fs
+++ b/forth/device/pathres.fs
@@ -290,6 +290,8 @@ constant sinfo.size
     interpose-args 2@ r@ >si.arguments 2!
     r@ link-one
     true my-self >in.interposed !
+    \ an interposed package answers my-unit for the device it sits on
+    my-self >in.my-parent @ >in.my-unit my-self >in.my-unit 4 cells move
     interpose-args 2@ free-mem
     r@ invoke-open
 
